- Treasury Management Indicators","url":"https://moderngov.oadby-wigston.gov.uk/documents/s36940/appendix-5-treasury-management-indicators.pdf","committee":"Policy, Finance & Development Committee","date":"16/06/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-29","committee":"Full Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.oadby-wigston.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-07","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.oadby-wigston.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-07","committee":"Full Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed; Special | Conferment of Title of Honorary Alderwoman","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.oadby-wigston.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-07","committee":"Full Council","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.oadby-wigston.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-30","committee":"Full Council","time":"8.00 pm","status":"Confirmed; Extraordinary | Local Government Reorganisation","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.oadby-wigston.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Policy, Finance & Development Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.oadby-wigston.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Full Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed; Extraordinary | Town/Parish Councils","webcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.oadby-wigston.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Business Rates Retention Reserve has a funding adjustment draw of \u00a3282,651 in addition to \u00a350,709 budgeted usage, totalling \u00a3333,360 drawdown","lead":"Business rates retention is how councils benefit from local economic growth. A significant reduction in this reserve suggests either the council is using reserves to cover shortfalls in retained business rates income, or it has planned a major drawdown to\u2026","iso":"2026-09-08","paper_title":"Appendix 3 - Statement of Movement on Reserves","paper_url":"https://moderngov.oadby-wigston.gov.uk/documents/s38208/38208.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"The \u00a3315,000 added to Contingency Reserve matches exactly the \u00a3315,000 drawn from LGR Reserve, suggesting either an undeclared transfer or classification inconsistency","lead":"Accounting consistency matters to lenders. If a transfer is being classified as both a budgeted addition and an unbudgeted draw, it raises questions about budget governance, management clarity, and reliability of the forecast.","iso":"2026-09-08","paper_title":"Appendix 3 - Statement of Movement on Reserves","paper_url":"https://moderngov.oadby-wigston.gov.uk/documents/s38208/38208.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Multiple unbudgeted reserve draws totalling at least \u00a3909,588 in 2026/27 indicate forecast errors or budget pressures","lead":"A lender needs to understand whether these unbudgeted draws represent one-off costs or a structural budget gap. Sustained reserve draws erode financial resilience and indicate a council operating beyond its means.","iso":"2026-09-08","paper_title":"Appendix 3 - Statement of Movement on Reserves","paper_url":"https://moderngov.oadby-wigston.gov.uk/documents/s38208/38208.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Policy, Finance & Development Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 3 - Statement of Movement on Reserves","paper_url":"https://moderngov.oadby-wigston.gov.uk/documents/s38208/38208.pdf","headline":"Business Rates Retention Reserve has a funding adjustment draw of \u00a3282,651 in addition to \u00a350,709 budgeted usage, totalling \u00a3333,360 drawdown","detail":"The Business Rates Retention Reserve (opening \u00a3743,526) is subject to both budgeted usage of \u00a350,709 and a funding adjustment of \u00a3282,651, leaving only \u00a3410,167 closing balance. This is a material reduction in a key source of council income flexibility.","category":"income","matters":"Business rates retention is how councils benefit from local economic growth. A significant reduction in this reserve suggests either the council is using reserves to cover shortfalls in retained business rates income, or it has planned a major drawdown to fund expenditure.","figures":"Business Rates Retention Reserve opening \u00a3743,526, budgeted usage \u00a350,709, funding adjustment \u00a3282,651, closing \u00a3410,167","quote":"Business Rates Retention Reserve (743,526) (743,526) 50,709 282,651 (410,167)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Policy, Finance & Development Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 3 - Statement of Movement on Reserves","paper_url":"https://moderngov.oadby-wigston.gov.uk/documents/s38208/38208.pdf","headline":"The \u00a3315,000 added to Contingency Reserve matches exactly the \u00a3315,000 drawn from LGR Reserve, suggesting either an undeclared transfer or classification inconsistency","detail":"Contingency Reserve is being increased by \u00a3315,000 (budgeted addition, opening \u00a3119,550 to closing \u00a3434,550), while LGR Reserve shows an unbudgeted draw of exactly \u00a3315,000 from a zero opening balance (closing -\u00a3315,000). The identical figure suggests movement between reserves rather than independent budget pressures, but the different classification (budgeted vs unbudgeted) is unusual.","category":"governance","matters":"Accounting consistency matters to lenders. If a transfer is being classified as both a budgeted addition and an unbudgeted draw, it raises questions about budget governance, management clarity, and reliability of the forecast.","figures":"Contingency Reserve budgeted addition \u00a3315,000; LGR Reserve unbudgeted usage \u00a3315,000 (exact match)","quote":"Contingency Reserve: Budgeted Additions/Useage in 2026/27 (315,000) closing (434,550); LGR Reserve: 0 opening, (315,000) Unbudgeted Useage, (315,000) closing","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Policy, Finance & Development Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 3 - Statement of Movement on Reserves","paper_url":"https://moderngov.oadby-wigston.gov.uk/documents/s38208/38208.pdf","headline":"Multiple unbudgeted reserve draws totalling at least \u00a3909,588 in 2026/27 indicate forecast errors or budget pressures","detail":"The statement shows significant unbudgeted reserve usage across multiple funds: LGR Reserve \u00a3315,000; EPR Reserve \u00a3131,601; General Fund Reserve \u00a363,987; and broader General Fund Earmarked Reserves showing \u00a3520,000 unbudgeted usage. These unbudgeted draws suggest the 2026/27 budget forecast did not hold, and the council is using reserves to cover the shortfall.","category":"reserves","matters":"A lender needs to understand whether these unbudgeted draws represent one-off costs or a structural budget gap. Sustained reserve draws erode financial resilience and indicate a council operating beyond its means.","figures":"LGR Reserve unbudgeted usage \u00a3315,000; EPR Reserve unbudgeted \u00a3131,601; General Fund Earmarked Reserves unbudgeted usage \u00a3520,000; General Fund Reserve unbudgeted usage \u00a363,987","quote":"Unbudgeted Useage in 2026/27: (520,000) for Total GF Earmarked Reserves; LGR Reserve: (315,000); EPR Reserve: 131,601 as unbudgeted; General Fund Reserve: (63,987)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Policy, Finance & Development Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 5 - Treasury Management Indicators","paper_url":"https://moderngov.oadby-wigston.gov.uk/documents/s38210/38210.pdf","headline":"Gross borrowing revised upward by \u00a31m without explanation","detail":"The council's gross borrowing forecast for 2026/27 was revised from \u00a335.683m to \u00a336.683m\u2014a \u00a31m increase (2.8%) compared to the original estimate. The document does not explain the reason for this revision, though it confirms the council will remain within its Capital Financing Requirement and the S151 Officer reports no difficulties foreseen.","category":"borrowing","matters":"An unexplained increase in projected borrowing need may indicate higher-than-expected capital costs or programme changes that warrant clarification when assessing financial sustainability and debt trajectory.","figures":"Gross Borrowing: 35,683 to 36,683 (\u00a3000s)","quote":"Gross Borrowing 35,683  36,683","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Policy, Finance & Development Committee","paper_title":"Budget Monitoring (Q1 2026/27)","paper_url":"https://moderngov.oadby-wigston.gov.uk/documents/s38205/38205.pdf","headline":"General Fund reserve buildup cut by 81% as overspends compress planned contributions","detail":"The council budgeted to build reserves by \u00a3337k in 2026/27 but will now only add \u00a364k\u2014a reduction of \u00a3273k (81%). While the absolute reserve balance grows to \u00a31.517m, the ability to strengthen financial resilience is severely impaired.","category":"reserves","matters":"Inability to build reserves at planned rate indicates the council is consuming financial headroom to balance the current year; slower reserve accumulation reduces capacity to absorb future shocks from homelessness, interest rates, or other pressures.","figures":"Budgeted reserve contribution \u00a3337k; forecast contribution \u00a364k; variance (\u00a3273k); opening reserve \u00a31.453m","quote":"The General fund outturn is expected to be a surplus of \u00a364k, as opposed to the \u00a3337k surplus that was budgeted for.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-08"},"name":"Oadby & Wigston","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-24","since_iso":"2026-08-25","distress":false,"headline":"Business Rates Retention Reserve has a funding adjustment draw of \u00a3282,651 in addition to \u00a350,709 budgeted usage, totalling \u00a3333,360 drawdown","lead":"